### Frontend ###
# Restored by `npm ci` from package-lock.json, which IS committed — that lockfile is what makes
# the build reproducible, so it must never be ignored.
dashboard/node_modules/
# Vite builds straight into target/classes/static during `mvn package`; nothing to keep here.
dashboard/dist/
dashboard/.vite/
npm-debug.log*
# frontend-maven-plugin downloads its own Node into target/, which is already ignored.

### Local Docker volumes ###
# PostgreSQL's data directory, bind-mounted by docker-compose. Thousands of
# binary files, machine-specific, and it would be a data leak if committed.
# Recreate from scratch with: docker compose down && rm -rf volumes/postgres
volumes/

### Secrets and local config ###
# This service ships deliberately fake keys (sk_test_demo_us_secret and friends)
# because it never touches real money. These rules exist so that if it is ever
# pointed at something real — a sandbox acquirer, a test Stripe account — the
# credentials cannot be committed by accident. A key leaked into git history is
# effectively permanent: rewriting history does not help once it has been pushed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
application-local.*
application-secrets.*
*-local.yml
*-local.yaml
*-local.properties
secrets/
credentials.json

# Keys and certificates
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
*.truststore

